 :org/countries ["GB" "IE" "AU" "BE" "PL" "DE"]
 :org/founding-date 1862
 :org/founding-note "The Working Men's Club and Institute Union was founded in 1862; miners' welfare institutes were funded by a levy on coal output from 1920."
 :org/member-count-basis "unknown and falling fast — CIU-affiliated clubs numbered in the thousands at mid-century and in the hundreds now; each club keeps its own membership book and no current national total is published."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "Member-owned social clubs with a bar, a committee and a subscription, built by industrial workforces to own their own leisure — and closing at a rate that tracks the disappearance of the industries that built them."
 :org/related-org "org-usa-legacy-fraternal-orders"
 :org/coverage-note "Recorded partly as a decline case: this is one of the clearest instances of a community form dying with its economic base."
